      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'The process starts with your certified divorce judgment from the Personal Status Court, attested at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MOFAIC). You then apply to ICP (Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs and Ports Security) to update your Emirates ID, then your home country embassy to update your passport, then the Roads and Transport Authority for your driving licence, and then update bank accounts, tenancy contracts, and employer records in sequence.',
