      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'My passport is in my husband\'s family name. How do I revert it to my maiden name?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'This is a home country matter, not a UAE one. The UAE cannot change what your passport says; only your embassy or national authority can. First check whether your nationality reverts you automatically once the divorce is registered at home, or whether you must apply. Some countries require the divorce to be recorded in their own civil registry before they issue an amended passport. Once the new passport is issued, bring it to ICP so your Emirates ID and residence visa point to the new document.',
