  { step: '05', institution: 'GDRFA / ICA', action: 'Update UAE residence visa', fee: 'Usually auto-updated', timeline: 'Automatic in most cases after Emirates ID update', notes: 'Check your visa status if on an employer or family visa' },
  { step: '06', institution: 'RTA (Dubai) / Transport authority', action: 'Update driving licence', fee: 'AED 100', timeline: 'Same day (walk-in)', notes: 'Bring updated Emirates ID + divorce certificate' },
  { step: '07', institution: 'Bank(s)', action: 'Update account name and marital status', fee: 'Usually no fee', timeline: '1-5 business days per bank', notes: 'Each bank has its own form; expect to visit a branch' },
  { step: '08', institution: 'Ejari / Tawtheeq', action: 'Update tenancy contract', fee: 'AED 100-200', timeline: '1-3 business days', notes: 'Required for Ejari re-registration in Dubai; Tawtheeq in Abu Dhabi' },
  { step: '09', institution: 'RTA (vehicles)', action: 'Update vehicle registration', fee: 'AED 50-100', timeline: 'Same day', notes: 'Bring updated Emirates ID + updated driving licence' },
  { step: '10', institution: 'Employer / HR', action: 'Update employment records', fee: 'None', timeline: 'Varies by employer', notes: 'May trigger need for new employment visa if name change is material' },
  { step: '11', institution: 'Children\'s schools', action: 'Update parent/guardian records', fee: 'None', timeline: '1-5 business days', notes: 'Bring updated Emirates ID + divorce certificate for school files' },
  { step: '12', institution: 'Health insurance provider', action: 'Update policy details', fee: 'None', timeline: '3-10 business days', notes: 'Ensure beneficiary records also updated' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'Do I have to change my name after divorce in UAE?',
    answer: 'No. Name reversion is entirely optional. There is no UAE law requiring you to revert to your maiden name. Many women choose to keep their married name for professional or family reasons. See our <a href="/en/divorce-timeline-uae/">divorce timeline guide</a> for what the court process does and does not automatically change.',
  },
  {
    question: 'I want to keep my married name but update my marital status. What do I need to update?',
    answer: 'You still need to update your Emirates ID to reflect "divorced" rather than "married", this is the core document. Your residence visa status may also need attention depending on your sponsorship. Bank accounts and tenancy contracts may need to be updated if they list "married" as a condition. Your passport and driving licence do not need updating if the name is unchanged.',
  },
  {
    question: 'My divorce was finalised abroad. Can I still update my UAE documents?',
    answer: 'Yes, but the foreign divorce certificate must be attested. For a UAE-resident updating UAE documents on the basis of a foreign divorce: have the certificate attested by the relevant ministry in the country of issue, then by the UAE embassy in that country, then by MOFAIC in UAE. Once attested and translated into Arabic, the process is the same as for a UAE court judgment. See our <a href="/en/divorce-certificate-attestation-uae/">divorce certificate attestation guide</a>.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens to my UAE residence visa after divorce?',
    answer: 'If your visa was sponsored by your spouse, you will need a new sponsorship once the divorce is finalised. Options include: employer sponsorship, a parent sponsorship, sponsoring yourself through a UAE freelance or company licence, or applying for the UAE Golden Visa if you qualify. You typically have 30 days after the sponsor cancels the visa to find new sponsorship or exit. See our <a href="/en/visa-after-divorce-uae/">visa after divorce UAE guide</a> for the full picture.',
  },
  {
    question: 'I changed my name before the divorce was registered. Is the divorce certificate in my old name?',
    answer: 'The divorce certificate will reference the name under which you were registered at marriage. If you changed your name by deed poll or other mechanism during the marriage, you may need additional documentation linking your two names. Consult your home country embassy as well as an Arabic-certified translator to ensure the documents are consistent.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I change my children\'s surname to my maiden name?',
    answer: 'Only with the father\'s consent or a court order. UAE courts require both parents\' agreement for a child\'s surname change and will not order a change against a parent\'s objection without compelling welfare grounds. This is a high threshold. If you and your ex-spouse agree, the change can be processed through the relevant registry with the divorce judgment and joint consent documentation.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I update my Ejari tenancy contract after divorce?',
    answer: 'In Dubai, Ejari is managed by the Dubai Land Department. You will need to re-register the tenancy contract in your updated name with an updated Emirates ID. If the lease was in your ex-spouse\'s name, you will need either a new lease agreement or an assignment of the existing lease, both require the landlord\'s agreement. Allow AED 100-200 for re-registration fees.',
  },
